## Why This Is Asked
This asks for a concrete governance approach to align many teams around data contracts, versioning, and regulatory constraints, a frequent real-world pain point in fintech.

## Key Concepts
- Contract driven development
- Data contracts and API versioning
- Cross team governance and automation
- Compliance and incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal contract validation skeleton
function validateContract(data, contract) {
  for (const field of contract.requiredFields) {
    if (data[field] === undefined) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure success and roll out across more teams?
- What are risks and mitigations for contract churn and migration?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates how a manager translates reliability goals into a concrete plan, balancing speed and risk, across teams and regions.

## Key Concepts
- SLOs and SLIs for latency and errors
- Incident response and runbooks
- Canary deployments and feature flags
- Tail latency and multi-region observability
- Instrumentation, profiling, and postmortems

## Code Example
```javascript
function percentile(arr, p){
  if (arr.length===0) return 0;
  const s = arr.slice().sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const idx = Math.floor((p/100)*(s.length-1));
  return s[idx];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you triage if p95 spikes are caused by an upstream service?
- How would you communicate risk to leadership during an incident?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates the ability to design governance that aligns regulatory requirements with product velocity in a distributed, multi-region setup.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-domain decision rights and escalation paths
- SLOs/SLIs, error budgets, runbooks, postmortems
- Phased releases: canary, shadow traffic, regional residency checks
- Rollback strategies and incident playbooks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-gating check for progress
function canProceed(region, changes) {
  if (!regsVerified(region)) return false;
  if (latencyImpact(changes) > SLO.latency) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate regulatory verification across regions?
- How would you handle conflicting gate criteria between regions?
